g issues and fix them. The problem is likely with Chinese punctuation being misinterpreted.\n\nLet me rewrite the problematic lines. Actually, let me just fix the specific lines and rerun.\n\nWait, the error is at line 499. Let me look at what's on that line in the file. The output says:\n```\n  File \"C:\\Users\\27063\\Desktop\\工具箱\\translate_srt.py\", line 499\n    \"这就像指路时说的：\"你一直开，直到看到那扇门，\",\n                   ^\nSyntaxError: invalid character '，' (U+FF0C)\n```\n\nThe `^` is pointing at `'` (the start of `'你一直开`). Wait no, it points at the first character of the line after the opening `\"`. The caret seems to be under `\"` (the LEFT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK U+201C).\n\nI think the issue is that the Chinese left curly double quote `\"` (U+201C) is being interpreted by Python as a regular quote, thus ending the string at that point, and then `你一直开，直到看到那扇门，` becomes invalid Python code with the fullwidth comma being the problematic character.\n\nBut U+201C and U+0022 are different characters... unless the file was written with ASCII quotes instead of curly quotes.\n\nThe simplest fix: replace `\"...\"` (curly quotes) with single angle quotes `'...'` or use `\\u201c` and `\\u201d` escape sequences, or just use a different convention.\n\nLet me just fix the problematic lines in the script. I'll replace the Chinese double quotes with `「」` corner brackets which won't conflict with Python string delimiters."}
